Given, $\frac{\Delta V}{V}=-0.4 \%=\frac{0.4}{100}$ Pressure required, $p=B \left(-\frac{\Delta V}{V}\right)
\begin{aligned}
& =\frac{0.4}{100} \times 2 \times 10^9 \mathrm{ Pa}=\frac{0.4}{100} \times \frac{2 \times 10^9}{101325} \mathrm{ atm} \\
& =79 \mathrm{ atm} \approx 80 \mathrm{ atm}
\end{aligned} Hence, 80 atm pressure is needed$ to compress a sample of water by 0.4 \%.

